# Volkswagen Polo Mk1 (Typ 86) three-door hatchback, 1976-1981.
#
# The first Polo: a short three-door hatch on the Audi 50 body, with a
# full-width black grille carrying two round headlamps, chrome bumpers and a
# bonded rear quarter window. Pre-facelift body (round lamps, metal bumpers);
# the 1979-81 facelift with square lamps and plastic bumpers is not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volkswagen_Polo_Mk1
#
# Dimensions 3.512 x 1.560 x 1.344 m, wheelbase 2.335 m (German Wikipedia
# infobox; not confirmed against a period UK road test).
#
# Shape reference: the side image is a true level side elevation but the car
# carries wheel-arch extensions, non-standard alloy wheels and a side stripe.
# The roofline, window line and door apertures are taken from it; the arches,
# wheels and ride height are standard. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: no UK brochure or price list was read, so no factory name is
# claimed (grade d). White, Red, Green and Blue are plain colour names. Weights
# 5, 4, 3, 3, total 15, reflecting about 86,000 UK sales over six years,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 135 km/h. Comfort 45/398, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 45. Classes 1,2.
# Dates 1976-1981 production, road tail staggered 1996-1998.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk1.dae. References: citycars/references/vw-polo-mk1/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0).
#
# Accepted deviations: the side photograph is a modified car; standard arches,
# steel wheels with hubcaps and standard ride height are modelled, with the
# hatch slope taken from the photographs rather than the brief's summary. The
# grille, bumper and badge detail are simplified, and the hatch perimeter seam
# and badges are omitted at sprite scale. Door shut lines are modelled.


obj=citycar
name=VWPoloMk1(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=5
intro_year=1976
intro_month=2
retire_year=1998
retire_month=6
speed=135
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=45
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=398

